course: dictionary
lesson: 11265
title: Wreath: a ring of flowers or smoke
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A wreath is a ring. Look at the words around it to see what kind. «Advent is the four weeks before Christmas, a time of waiting and getting ready, with Advent wreaths and calendars.» The clues are Christmas and getting ready, so a wreath is a decoration for the season.
explain: «Girls float flower wreaths on the water at midsummer.» You cannot float a fat block of wood, but flowers can float, so a flower wreath is a ring of flowers. Try the swap: put «a ring of flowers» into the sentence. It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Wreath also has a second meaning. «A wreath of mist hung over the lake.» Mist cannot be made of flowers, so here a wreath is a ring or curl of mist. Always check the clues before you choose a meaning.
fact: A wreath is a ring of flowers, leaves or branches.
fact: People use wreaths as decoration, such as a Christmas wreath on a door.
fact: Wreaths are also laid to remember people who have died, such as poppy wreaths on remembrance days for soldiers.
fact: In ancient games, winners wore laurel wreaths on their heads.
fact: A wreath of smoke or mist is a ring or curl of it. The verb wreathe means to wind round or cover, as in «mist wreathed the hills».
exercise: «Advent is the four weeks before Christmas, with Advent wreaths and calendars.» What is a wreath? | *A ring of flowers, leaves or branches | A present under a pillow | A candle that burns for a week | A kind of calendar
exercise: «Girls float flower wreaths on the water at midsummer.» What does wreath mean here? | A small wooden boat | A bonfire on the beach | *A ring of flowers | A fishing net
exercise: «A wreath of mist hung over the lake.» What does wreath mean in this sentence? | A flower decoration on a door | A heavy stone wall | A straight stick of mist | *A ring or curl of mist
test: Why do people lay a wreath at a funeral or on remembrance day? | To show that it is a sunny day | *To remember someone who has died | To count the guests | To keep the flowers cool
test: What is a laurel wreath? | *A wreath won as a prize in an ancient game | A flower wreath floated on water | A poppy wreath laid for soldiers | A wreath of holly for Christmas
exam: Which sentence uses wreath to mean a ring or curl of smoke or mist? | «She hung a holly wreath on the front door.» | *«A wreath of smoke rose slowly from the chimney.» | «The children floated flower wreaths on the river.» | «The wreath of poppies was laid at the memorial.»
